  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Food Security and Resilience of Rural Communities in Sudan (Netherlands Red Cross)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Around 60,000 people in Kassala and Northern States, Sudan, including IDPs. This includes:
1) approximately 30,000 people in 15 communities in Al Golid Locality, Northern State (the same target communities as in the previous DG INTPA-funded GCCA+ action between 2017-2022)
2) approximately 30.000 people in 15 communities in Aroma town, Kassala State. The new communities in Aroma town will be selected based on high cases of malnutrition and vulnerability to natural hazards such as flooding.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Northern and Kassala states, Sudan</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sudan faces a serious hunger crisis, ranking 106th out of 121 countries in the 2022 Global Hunger Index. By December 2023, an estimated 19 million people are expected to experience acute food insecurity. The situation is dire, with 95% of households spending more than 65% of their total income on food. The impacts of climate change, including increased climate variability and more frequent and intense droughts, are evident throughout the country. Additionally, since mid-April 2023, a violent conflict has erupted, significantly exacerbating humanitarian needs.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project objectives will be achieved by strengthening the capacity of the smallholders and adopting climate smart-techniques to scale-up yields, stabilize food systems, improve food security, and reduce vulnerabilities to climate-related risks. As rural livelihoods depend on natural resources as key inputs (water, soil, grazing) to ensure yields, the intervention will also improve the health of key natural resources and (shared) management of natural resources, as well as work towards ensuring equal and sustainable access to natural resources as means of food production.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will contribute to strengthening communities&#x2019; food security through improved production and the adoption of climate-smart practices as well as to contribute to equal and sustainable access to natural resources.</narrative>
  </description>
